{uncertain: 'kano kraj mulca': mulac is not a common word; read as 'mule' (rhyme with vujca), marked (?) in the translation. Needs a speaker of the dialect.}
{uncertain: 'A šta ću ti ja?' is idiomatic: 'And what can I do about it?' / 'What good is that to me?'.}
{uncertain: The old PDF of 19.11.2026 had the words of a different song ('Dremle mi se, dremle, na krovu golobek'); replaced with Pjesme tekstovi.pdf.}
{uncertain: Meter 3/4 measured on the drums stem (periodicity at 3 and 6 beats); the frame-drum strokes D T T are the plain 3/4 pattern, to be confirmed by the professor.}

{section: 1}
[Dm]Dremle mi [G]se, mi[Dm]la maj[G]ko, || I'm so sleepy, dear mother,
[Dm]spavala bi [C]ja. [Am] || I would like to sleep.
[Dm]Legni, [G]kćeri, [Dm]pokraj [G]vujca. || Lie down, daughter, beside your uncle.
[Dm]A šta [F]ću ti [C]ja? [Am] || And what can I do?

[Dm]Legla kraj [G]vujca [Dm]kano [G]kraj mulca, || I lay beside my uncle as if beside a mule (?),
[Dm]zima je [C]meni. [Am] || I am cold.
[Dm]Nit [G]zagrljena, [Dm]nit polju[G]bljena, || Neither embraced nor kissed,
[Dm]zima [F]je [C]meni. [Am] || I am cold.

{section: 2}
